T002 substring: a case-sensitive match -> the filter matches a case-insensitive substring: APP keeps app-counter, and app
T002 nothing matched: a name completed from framework knowledge -> the filter never completes a name from framework knowledge: a query for the framework’s app-root keeps nothing, because this record does not carry it
T002 rows: a row the record does not carry -> the filter emits no row the record does not carry, and copies the count the record states | a count the record does not state -> a count the record does not state is null, never a count the record lacks
T002 cannot-tell: a cause the record invented, repeated as though measured -> the filter never repeats a cause the record invented: the reason is a member of the closed set
E4 empty beside cannot-tell: empty reported where the source is unreadable -> an unreadable source is cannot-tell with its reason, never an empty list presented as a result
T002 idempotency: rows reordered out of the record’s order -> identical rows in identical order, in the order the record carries them
T002 one implementation: the list is read from the record, and no caller reads the DOM to build it
T002 closed set: 5 reasons, 2 of them the filter’s own
